      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Replay adds a fraction of general text to the new domain stream. Its purpose is to keep selected broad examples contributing to the same next-token objective. A token-counted replay share can differ from a document-counted share when examples have different lengths.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 16.312,
          "duration": 15.912,
          "until": 16.862
        },
        {
          "say": "Restore this same shared logit to zero before each controlled mixture comparison. In a one-parameter teaching model, domain examples push the logit upward and replay examples push it downward. At a quarter replay, the weighted gradient changes from minus point five to minus point two five.",
          "start": 16.862,
          "end": 34.45399999999999,
          "duration": 17.592,
          "until": 35.004
        },
        {
          "say": "That arithmetic explains the mixture; a useful replay percentage depends on the model and the measured capabilities to preserve. The fraction of scored tokens matters, and separate domain-only and replay-only controls help interpret results.",
